TIP:  In the intro and outro try playing the (DaddA) for the first three sets of the (D) chord.  (DaddA) is just (D) with your pinky extended to cover the 1st string of the 5th fret.  You can play regular (D) but the (DaddA) gets the treble <a> note in there which is what Vince is playing.  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (DaddA) and add the 5th note as needed.

TIP:  The strumming pattern is quick and for each bar/measure is down, down up down up down up/ down, down up down up down up . . . with first downstroke coming on each chord in a new bar and/or chord change.


